<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31760" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏboedĭentĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obed-</span></b> ), ae,
			f.
		oboediens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>obedience</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of persons. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> With <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servitus est oboedientia fracti animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Par. 5, 1, 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">relinquunt enim et abiciunt oboedientiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 1, 29</span></i>
			. 102.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Of bees: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mira plebi circa regem oboedientia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 17, 17, § 52</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> Of
			elephants: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intellectus illis sermonis patrii et imperiorum
					oboedientia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 8,
					1, 1, § 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
